      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I also think that this Launchpad update is not a good one.\n\nTo summarize briefly:\n\nDon't move important buttons too frequently.\n\nDon't make important buttons smaller.\n\nDon't remove the expand button.\n\nDon't leave too much white space.\n\nYou should judge the importance of a button based on how many times you press it.\n\nYou should carefully align what users need with what the management wants them to use.\n\nAnother way to put it is this:The menu from about a year ago is better. \n\nI thought that criticism alone would only complicate the situation, so I only made the bare minimum changes and created an image as an example of a better design.\n\nI've posted it alongside the current version for easy comparison.\n\nI believe there are many areas that could be improved if we carefully honed them in on them, but I intentionally kept the changes to a minimum.\n\nSystem overhauls are important at times, but innovation without user support is simply destructive. If the person who created this UI arbitrarily swapped the back and home buttons on the smartphone, and changed the PC keyboard from QWERTY to AZERTY, or vice versa, would people understand how inconvenient it would be?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
